  "query_preview": "/Monday through Friday/...\nIssued 401 AM MDT FRI JUL 31 2026\nContinued upper-level troughing over southern Canada is expected\nto temper the Desert Southwest ridge from building too far into\nthe region. This will result in weak westerly flow aloft. A steady drying \ntrend will continue, with lower elevation temperatures returning\nto the mid 90s by Wednesday and Thursday. Winds will subside \ncompared to the weekend, returning to typical afternoon breezy \nconditions. Additionally, PWAT values will drop under the 10th \npercentile climatology across the region, with values near 0.3 \ninches Monday through Thursday. This will cause precipitation \nchances to remain near zero across southeast Oregon and \nsouthwest Idaho. Several large fires across eastern Oregon will\ncontinue to spread smoke across western Idaho, thus, smoky \nconditions are likely to persist through the end of the week.",
